  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-142519",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The parallel line segments $\\overset{―}{CD}∥\\overset{―}{AF}$ are cut by the transversal $\\overset{―}{AD}.$\n\nThe angles $∠ODC$ and $∠FAO$ are interior to the parallel line segments and are on opposite sides of the transversal. So, they are alternate interior angles and consequently, they have the same measure.\n\nIn step 4, we found that $m∠ODC=5{x}^{∘}.$\n\nSetting the measures of $∠ODC$ and $∠FAO$ equal to each other, we have an equation that we can solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ODC & =m∠FAO \\\\ 5{x}^{∘} & =(3x+18)^{∘} \\\\ 5x & =3x+18 \\\\ 2x & =18 \\\\ x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=9$ into the expressions for the measures of $∠FAO$ and $∠AOE$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠FAO & =(3x+18)^{∘} \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 9+18)^{∘} \\\\  & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOE & =(185-5x)^{∘} \\\\  & =(185-5\\cdot 9)^{∘} \\\\  & ={140}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $m∠FAO={45}^{∘}$ and $m∠AOE={140}^{∘}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
